[Event "Ruy Lopez for White"]
[Lesson "spanish-idea"]
[LessonTitle "The idea of the Ruy Lopez"]
[Step "explain"]
[TeacherNotes "The Ruy Lopez is also called the Spanish Game | The bishop does not win a pawn at once. It adds slow pressure | The knight on c6 guards the e5 pawn, so pressure on c6 is pressure on e5 | Ask: what could White do on e5 if the c6 knight went away?"]
[Mistakes "Thinking Bb5 threatens to win the knight right now. It does not, because the knight is defended | Trading on c6 without a plan | Forgetting to castle after the bishop move"]
[ClassQuestions "Which black piece does the bishop on b5 point at? | Which black pawn does that knight protect? | Why is slow pressure still useful?"]

{The idea in one sentence: the bishop pressures the knight on c6, which guards the e5 pawn. [%cal Gb5c6,Yc6e5] [%csl Rc6,Ye5]}
1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 {Now the knight on c6 is under pressure. For now it is safe, but White plays for the long game. [%cal Gb5c6]} *

[Event "Ruy Lopez for White"]
[Lesson "spanish-idea"]
[Step "find-move"]
[FEN "r1bqkbnr/pppp1ppp/2n5/4p3/4P3/5N2/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKB1R w KQkq - 2 3"]
[Hint "Use your bishop on f1."]
[Hint "Move it to b5, so it points at the knight on c6."]

{White to move. Start the Ruy Lopez: put the bishop on the square that pressures the c6 knight.}
3. Bb5 {The Ruy Lopez. [%cal Gb5c6]} *

[Event "Ruy Lopez for White"]
[Lesson "spanish-idea"]
[Step "explain"]

{The bishop on b5 looks along a diagonal at the knight on c6. That knight guards the e5 pawn.}
1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 *

[Event "Ruy Lopez for White"]
[Lesson "morphy-defence"]
[LessonTitle "Morphy Defence: 3...a6"]
[Step "explain"]
[TeacherNotes "3...a6 is the most common reply. It is called the Morphy Defence | Black asks the bishop what it wants to do | Retreating to a4 keeps the pressure on c6 | After 5.O-O White is ready; the e4 pawn is not a worry yet"]
[Mistakes "4.Bxc6 is the Exchange Variation, a different plan; 4.Ba4 keeps the tension. | Moving the bishop to c4 and losing the pressure on c6 | Leaving the king in the middle"]
[ClassQuestions "What is the little pawn on a6 asking the bishop? | Why is a4 a good retreat? | Why do we castle on move five?"]

{Black asks the bishop a question with 3...a6. White's answer is to keep the bishop on the same diagonal. [%cal Ra6b5,Gb5a4]}
1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 {The Morphy Defence.} 4. Ba4 {The bishop retreats but still points at c6. [%cal Ga4c6]} 4... Nf6 {Black attacks the e4 pawn. [%cal Rf6e4]} 5. O-O {White castles and gets the king safe. [%cal Ge1g1]} *

[Event "Ruy Lopez for White"]
[Lesson "morphy-defence"]
[Step "find-move"]
[FEN "r1bqkbnr/1ppp1ppp/p1n5/1B2p3/4P3/5N2/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK2R w KQkq - 0 4"]
[Hint "Use your bishop."]
[Hint "Move it one square along the same diagonal, to a4."]

{White to move. The pawn on a6 attacks your bishop. Retreat it one square along the same diagonal, so it still points at the c6 knight.}
4. Ba4 {The bishop is safe and keeps the pressure. [%cal Ga4c6]} *

[Event "Ruy Lopez for White"]
[Lesson "morphy-defence"]
[Step "find-move"]
[FEN "r1bqkb1r/1ppp1ppp/p1n2n2/4p3/B3P3/5N2/PPPP1PPP/RNBQK2R w KQkq - 2 5"]
[Hint "Use your king."]
[Hint "Castle on the short side, so the king goes to g1."]

{White to move. Get your king safe by castling.}
5. O-O {The king is safe and the rook comes to the middle. [%cal Ge1g1,Gh1f1]} *

[Event "Ruy Lopez for White"]
[Lesson "morphy-defence"]
[Step "line-drill"]
[Side "white"]
[Hint "Open with the king's pawn, then the knight, then the bishop to b5."]
[Hint "When the a-pawn asks, retreat the bishop to a4."]
[Hint "Finish by castling."]

{Play the Morphy Defence line as White.}
1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 Nf6 5. O-O *
